    "long_instructions": "# Practice Grading a Project\r\n\r\nLook over this sample student project, and think about how you will assess it. \r\n\r\nOn the next level, you'll grade a sample capstone project using the interactive rubric. Before you do, preview the full rubric criteria below so you know what you're looking for at each level.\r\n\r\n:::details [Project Planning & Intentional Design]\r\n- **No Evidence (1 pt):** Purpose, audience, or scope is missing or incoherent.\r\n- **Limited Evidence (2 pts):** Purpose or audience is vague, or scope is unclear or unrealistic. Little explanation of decisions.\r\n- **Convincing Evidence (3 pts):** Purpose and audience are clear. Scope is mostly realistic, with some explanation of decisions or changes made over time.\r\n- **Extensive Evidence (4 pts):** Clearly explains the project's purpose, audience, and problem. Scope decisions are realistic and intentional, with clear tradeoffs explained. Reflection shows how ideas or scope evolved over time.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [Functionality & Technical Implementation]\r\n- **No Evidence (1 pt):** App does not run or core functionality is missing.\r\n- **Limited Evidence (2 pts):** App works inconsistently or only partially. Logic is unclear or does not align well with intended behavior. Code structure is difficult to follow.\r\n- **Convincing Evidence (3 pts):** App works for the main use case. Logic generally matches intended behavior and functions as expected. Code is mostly readable and organized.\r\n- **Extensive Evidence (4 pts):** App runs reliably and supports its intended purpose. Logic clearly matches the intended system behavior and correctly handles user input and data. Code is organized, readable, and modular.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [User-Centered Design & Usability]\r\n- **No Evidence (1 pt):** No clear attention to usability or user needs.\r\n- **Limited Evidence (2 pts):** Design is confusing, inconsistent, or only loosely connected to user needs.\r\n- **Convincing Evidence (3 pts):** Design is generally clear and usable. Some evidence of considering user needs or feedback.\r\n- **Extensive Evidence (4 pts):** Design clearly supports the target audience. Interface choices improve clarity, usability, and trust. Feedback is reflected in design or interaction changes.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [Responsible AI & Ethical Reflection]\r\n- **No Evidence (1 pt):** No meaningful documentation of AI use or ethical thinking.\r\n- **Limited Evidence (2 pts):** Mentions AI use or ethics superficially, with limited reasoning.\r\n- **Convincing Evidence (3 pts):** Describes how AI was used and includes some reflection on ethical or design implications.\r\n- **Extensive Evidence (4 pts):** Clearly explains how AI tools were used. Reflection shows strong judgment in accepting, modifying, or rejecting AI output. Thoughtfully considers ethics, inclusion, or unintended impacts.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n:::details [Collaboration & Professional Practice]\r\n- **No Evidence (1 pt):** Little or no evidence of collaboration or professional process.\r\n- **Limited Evidence (2 pts):** Collaboration is uneven or unclear. Limited or inconsistent use of the Project Planning Board.\r\n- **Convincing Evidence (3 pts):** Demonstrates collaboration. Project Planning Board shows ongoing task tracking and iteration, with some evidence of shared ownership or communication.\r\n- **Extensive Evidence (4 pts):** Demonstrates effective collaboration and shared ownership. Project Planning Board shows ongoing task tracking, prioritization, and iteration, with clear communication and coordination over time.\r\n:::\r\n",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Use Web Lab to review and finalize the version of your app you are ready to share. This should reflect the decisions you are standing behind at this point in the project. ***(supports completing Milestone 5)***.",
