        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "contents": "body {\n  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n  background-color: #fdf6f0;\n  color: #2b2b2b;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n}\n\nheader {\n  background-color: #b5482f;\n  color: white;\n  padding: 24px 20px;\n  text-align: center;\n}\n\nheader h1 {\n  margin: 0 0 6px 0;\n}\n\nmain {\n  max-width: 700px;\n  margin: 0 auto;\n  padding: 20px;\n}\n\nsection {\n  background-color: white;\n  border: 1px solid #e8d9cf;\n  border-radius: 8px;\n  padding: 18px 20px;\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n\nh2 {\n  color: #b5482f;\n  margin-top: 0;\n}\n\n.list-columns {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 20px;\n}\n\n.list-column {\n  flex: 1;\n}\n\n.list-column h3 {\n  font-size: 15px;\n  color: #6b6b6b;\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\nul {\n  list-style: none;\n  padding: 0;\n  margin: 0;\n}\n\nli {\n  background-color: #f4ede6;\n  padding: 10px 12px;\n  margin-bottom: 8px;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\n\nli:hover {\n  background-color: #ecdccb;\n}\n\n#packed-list li {\n  background-color: #dff0d8;\n  text-decoration: line-through;\n  color: #4a7a4a;\n}\n\n#training-list li.complete {\n  background-color: #dff0d8;\n  text-decoration: line-through;\n  color: #4a7a4a;\n}\n\n#packing-counter, #training-counter {\n  font-weight: bold;\n  color: #b5482f;\n}\n\n#habitat-buttons {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 10px;\n  margin-bottom: 14px;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n}\n\n.habitat-btn {\n  padding: 12px 16px;\n  border: 2px solid #b5482f;\n  background-color: white;\n  color: #b5482f;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  font-size: 14px;\n}\n\n.habitat-btn:hover {\n  background-color: #fbeee7;\n}\n\n.habitat-btn.selected {\n  background-color: #b5482f;\n  color: white;\n}\n\n#habitat-description {\n  background-color: #f4ede6;\n  padding: 14px;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n#habitat-description ul {\n  margin: 8px 0 0 18px;\n  list-style: disc;\n}\n\n#habitat-description li {\n  background: none;\n  padding: 2px 0;\n  cursor: default;\n}\n\nfooter {\n  text-align: center;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  color: #8a8a8a;\n  padding: 20px;\n}\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "script.js",
          "contents": "// Packing list data\nvar packingItems = [\n  { id: 1, name: \"Water Filtration Kit\", packed: false },\n  { id: 2, name: \"Freeze-Dried Meals (7 days)\", packed: false },\n  { id: 3, name: \"Oxygen Backup Tank\", packed: false },\n  { id: 4, name: \"Radiation Suit\", packed: false },\n  { id: 5, name: \"Solar Panel Charger\", packed: false },\n  { id: 6, name: \"First Aid Kit\", packed: false },\n  { id: 7, name: \"Comm Radio\", packed: false },\n  { id: 8, name: \"Tool Kit\", packed: false }\n];\n\n// Training log data\nvar trainings = [\n  { id: 1, name: \"Zero-Gravity Movement\", complete: false },\n  { id: 2, name: \"Emergency Oxygen Protocol\", complete: false },\n  { id: 3, name: \"Habitat Systems Basics\", complete: false },\n  { id: 4, name: \"Rover Operation\", complete: false }\n];\n\n// Habitat data\nvar habitats = [\n  {\n    id: \"dome\",\n    name: \"Dome Habitat\",\n    details: [\n      \"Large shared living space\",\n      \"Good natural light through the dome panels\",\n      \"Harder to insulate against temperature swings\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"underground\",\n    name: \"Underground Habitat\",\n    details: [\n      \"Best protection from radiation\",\n      \"Stable temperature year-round\",\n      \"No natural light, feels cramped to some trainees\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"inflatable\",\n    name: \"Inflatable Habitat\",\n    details: [\n      \"Lightest and fastest to set up\",\n      \"Easy to expand later if needed\",\n      \"Less durable than the other two options\"\n    ]\n  }\n];\n\nvar selectedHabitat = null;\n\n// keeps clicks from double-firing and skipping a count\n// (found this during testing - see Testing Log in capstone.md)\nvar clickLocked = false;\n\nfunction renderPacking() {\n  var toPackList = document.getElementById(\"to-pack-list\");\n  var packedList = document.getElementById(\"packed-list\");\n  toPackList.innerHTML = \"\";\n  packedList.innerHTML = \"\";\n\n  var packedCount = 0;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < packingItems.length; i++) {\n    var item = packingItems[i];\n    var li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n    li.textContent = item.name;\n    li.addEventListener(\"click\", makePackingClickHandler(item.id));\n\n    if (item.packed) {\n      packedCount++;\n      packedList.appendChild(li);\n    } else {\n      toPackList.appendChild(li);\n    }\n  }\n\n  document.getElementById(\"packing-counter\").textContent =\n    packedCount + \" of \" + packingItems.length + \" packed\";\n}\n\nfunction makePackingClickHandler(id) {\n  return function () {\n    if (clickLocked) return;\n    clickLocked = true;\n\n    for (var i = 0; i < packingItems.length; i++) {\n      if (packingItems[i].id === id) {\n        packingItems[i].packed = !packingItems[i].packed;\n      }\n    }\n    renderPacking();\n\n    setTimeout(function () {\n      clickLocked = false;\n    }, 150);\n  };\n}\n\nfunction renderTraining() {\n  var list = document.getElementById(\"training-list\");\n  list.innerHTML = \"\";\n\n  var completeCount = 0;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < trainings.length; i++) {\n    var training = trainings[i];\n    var li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n    li.textContent = training.name;\n    if (training.complete) {\n      li.className = \"complete\";\n      completeCount++;\n    }\n    li.addEventListener(\"click\", makeTrainingClickHandler(training.id));\n    list.appendChild(li);\n  }\n\n  document.getElementById(\"training-counter\").textContent =\n    completeCount + \" of \" + trainings.length + \" complete\";\n}\n\nfunction makeTrainingClickHandler(id) {\n  return function () {\n    if (clickLocked) return;\n    clickLocked = true;\n\n    for (var i = 0; i < trainings.length; i++) {\n      if (trainings[i].id === id) {\n        trainings[i].complete = !trainings[i].complete;\n      }\n    }\n    renderTraining();\n\n    setTimeout(function () {\n      clickLocked = false;\n    }, 150);\n  };\n}\n\nfunction renderHabitatButtons() {\n  var container = document.getElementById(\"habitat-buttons\");\n  container.innerHTML = \"\";\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < habitats.length; i++) {\n    var habitat = habitats[i];\n    var btn = document.createElement(\"button\");\n    btn.className = \"habitat-btn\";\n    btn.textContent = habitat.name;\n    if (selectedHabitat === habitat.id) {\n      btn.className += \" selected\";\n    }\n    btn.addEventListener(\"click\", makeHabitatClickHandler(habitat.id));\n    container.appendChild(btn);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction makeHabitatClickHandler(id) {\n  return function () {\n    selectedHabitat = id;\n    renderHabitatButtons();\n    renderHabitatDescription();\n  };\n}\n\nfunction renderHabitatDescription() {\n  var descBox = document.getElementById(\"habitat-description\");\n\n  if (!selectedHabitat) {\n    descBox.textContent = \"Pick a habitat above to see the details.\";\n    return;\n  }\n\n  var habitat = null;\n  for (var i = 0; i < habitats.length; i++) {\n    if (habitats[i].id === selectedHabitat) {\n      habitat = habitats[i];\n    }\n  }\n\n  descBox.innerHTML = \"<strong>\" + habitat.name + \"</strong><ul></ul>\";\n  var ul = descBox.querySelector(\"ul\");\n  for (var j = 0; j < habitat.details.length; j++) {\n    var li = document.createElement(\"li\");\n    li.textContent = habitat.details[j];\n    ul.appendChild(li);\n  }\n}\n\nrenderPacking();\nrenderTraining();\nrenderHabitatButtons();\nrenderHabitatDescription();\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "4": {
          "id": "4",
          "name": "capstone.md",
          "contents": "# APP PLAN\n\n**App Name:** Red Planet Ready\n**Team:** Maya R. & Jordan T.\n\n## App Idea\nOur app is called Red Planet Ready. It's a checklist and training tracker for trainees getting ready for a simulated Mars mission at space camp. Right now trainees get their packing list, training schedule, and habitat info on three different paper handouts, and people lose them or forget what they've already done. Our app puts all three in one place so trainees can see their prep progress at a glance.\n\n## Audience\nOur audience is junior astronaut trainees (basically kids our age) who are getting ready for a multi-day Mars simulation at camp. They need this because the paper system makes it hard to know what's left to do, especially with three separate lists to track. A single digital checklist means they can check their status in one spot instead of digging through handouts.\n\n## Scope\n\n### What This Version Includes\n- A packing checklist where you can move items from \"To Pack\" to \"Packed\" and see a live counter\n- A training log where you can mark trainings as complete and see how many you've finished\n- A habitat picker where you choose between three habitat types and read a short description of each\n\n### What We Left Out (and Why)\nWe left out saving your progress between visits (like if you closed the tab and came back). We looked into using the browser's storage for this but ran out of time to get it working reliably, so for this version your checklist resets if you reload the page. We also decided not to let trainees make their own custom packing items — everyone uses the same list, which keeps it simpler and means we didn't have to build a way to add/delete items.\n\n## System\n\n### User Interaction Walkthrough\nHere's one complete interaction, from what the user does to what they see happen:\n\n- **User action:** Trainee clicks an item in the \"To Pack\" list, like \"Radiation Suit.\"\n- **App decision or logic:** The app finds that item in our packing list array and flips its `packed` value from `false` to `true`. Then it re-draws both the \"To Pack\" list and the \"Packed\" list based on the updated array, and recalculates the counter by counting how many items have `packed: true`.\n- **Result:** \"Radiation Suit\" disappears from \"To Pack\" and appears in \"Packed,\" and the counter updates from something like \"3 of 8 packed\" to \"4 of 8 packed.\"\n\nThe training log works the same way, just with a \"complete\" flag instead of \"packed.\"\n\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Testing Log\n\n**Test 1 (Day 4):** Clicked through the whole packing list to make sure every item could move to \"Packed\" and the counter matched. It worked, but we noticed if you clicked an item really fast twice in a row, the counter would sometimes skip a number. We fixed this by disabling the click for a split second after each one (there's a comment in script.js marking this).\n\n**Test 2 (Day 6):** Had a trainee from another team test the habitat picker. They found that nothing told you which habitat was currently selected once you clicked away from it — the description showed up but the button didn't look \"selected.\" We added a highlight style to the chosen habitat button to fix this.\n\n**Test 3 (Day 7):** Checked the training log on a smaller laptop screen and noticed the buttons were pretty small to tap accurately. We increased the padding on the buttons so they're easier to click, especially on trackpads.\n\nWe did not get to test on an actual phone screen, so we're not totally sure how it looks on mobile.\n\n---\n\n# FEEDBACK & ITERATION\n\n## Feedback Log\n\n**Feedback received:** Our Benchmark B peer reviewer said the habitat descriptions were kind of long and hard to skim, and suggested breaking them into short bullet points instead of paragraphs.\n\n**Change we made:** We rewrote the three habitat descriptions as short bullet lists (pros/cons style) instead of paragraphs. This made the picker feel a lot less overwhelming to read.\n\n**Feedback we didn't act on:** The same reviewer suggested adding pictures for each habitat option. We decided not to do this because we didn't have time to find images that matched our habitat descriptions accurately, and we didn't want to just grab random space images that didn't actually represent the habitat we described. We figured a clear written description was more honest than a stock photo that might not match.\n\n---\n\n# BENCHMARK REFLECTIONS\n\n## Benchmark A — Day 3\nAt this point we had our app idea, audience, and scope written out, but our system explanation was pretty rough — we hadn't actually decided how the packing list would be stored in code yet. Talking it through at benchmark A helped us settle on using one array of objects instead of separate variables for each item, which made the rest of the build a lot easier.\n\n## Benchmark B — Day 5\nBy benchmark B we had the packing checklist and training log working. The main thing we changed after this check-in was fixing the double-click counter bug from our testing log. We also realized our habitat picker wasn't started yet, so we moved it up in our Kanban board priority for the next few days.\n\n## Benchmark C — Day 8\nAt benchmark C we had all three features working and had gotten feedback on the habitat descriptions. We used this time to rewrite those descriptions into bullet points and clean up some of our CSS spacing that was inconsistent between the three sections.\n\n---\n\n# FINAL REFLECTION\n\n## How Our App Evolved\nWe started out just planning a packing checklist, but during Milestone 1 we realized trainees deal with three separate lists (packing, training, habitat choice), so we expanded scope to include all three in one app. The biggest change from testing was realizing our habitat picker needed a way to show what was currently selected, since our first version just showed the description with no visual confirmation.\n\n## Responsible AI Use\nWe used AI help twice during this project. First, when our double-click counter bug showed up, we described the bug to an AI tool and asked what might be causing it. It suggested adding a short delay/disable after each click, which we used, but we wrote the actual delay logic ourselves in a way that fit our existing code instead of pasting in what it gave us directly. Second, we asked an AI tool to check our habitat description bullet points for clarity after we rewrote them, and used a couple of its wording suggestions but kept our own structure. We tried to only use AI for feedback and troubleshooting, not to write features for us, since we wanted the logic in script.js to actually be ours.\n\n## Ready to Share\nOur app runs reliably for its main use case — packing checklist, training log, and habitat picker all work as intended. We haven't tested on mobile, so we'd want to check that before sharing publicly, but for an in-class or school showcase we feel ready to present.\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        },
        "5": {
          "id": "5",
          "name": "index.html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <title>Red Planet Ready</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n\n  <header>\n    <h1>🚀 Red Planet Ready</h1>\n    <p>Your Mars simulation prep, all in one place.</p>\n  </header>\n\n  <main>\n\n    <section id=\"packing-section\">\n      <h2>Packing Checklist</h2>\n      <p id=\"packing-counter\">0 of 8 packed</p>\n\n      <div class=\"list-columns\">\n        <div class=\"list-column\">\n          <h3>To Pack</h3>\n          <ul id=\"to-pack-list\"></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"list-column\">\n          <h3>Packed</h3>\n          <ul id=\"packed-list\"></ul>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"training-section\">\n      <h2>Training Log</h2>\n      <p id=\"training-counter\">0 of 4 complete</p>\n      <ul id=\"training-list\"></ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section id=\"habitat-section\">\n      <h2>Choose Your Habitat</h2>\n      <div id=\"habitat-buttons\"></div>\n      <div id=\"habitat-description\">Pick a habitat above to see the details.</div>\n    </section>\n\n  </main>\n\n  <footer>\n    <p>Built for the AI Foundations Capstone &mdash; Team Maya R. &amp; Jordan T.</p>\n  </footer>\n\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
